{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-action-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-action-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the categorical action (given $\\Phi$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-action-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-action-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","categorical-action"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalAction.unique","text":"categorical-action-unique.md","leanSource":"categorical-action-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-action-unique\"></a><p>For a fixed Lagrangian endomorphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi \\in \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A)</code> and transposition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{swap}</code>, the categorical action <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{S}_\\Phi = \\mathrm{ev}_A \\circ \\mathrm{swap} \\circ (\\Phi \\otimes \\mathrm{id}_{A^\\vee}) \\circ \\mathrm{coev}_A</code> does not depend on the choice of right dual of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>. If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(A, D_1)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(A, D_2)</code> are two exact pairings and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi \\colon D_1 \\xrightarrow{\\sim} D_2</code> is the canonical isomorphism between them, then computing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{S}_\\Phi</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_2</code> and the transported transposition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\varphi \\otimes \\mathrm{id}_A) \\circ \\mathrm{swap} \\circ (\\mathrm{id}_A \\otimes \\varphi^{-1})</code> gives the same morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{1} \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> as computing it with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_1</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{swap}</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.14.3","page":"b/prop-categorical-action-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":80},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.CategoricalAction.unique","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-action-unique.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
